     7	
     8	At Steps 4–5 draw 1440px **grayscale structure only**; wait for the recorded Step 5 approval before color/type styling. At Step 6 trace the single visual idea to brief lines, use [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), and name frames `<screen>/<state>/<version>`. Show default, hover, focus, disabled, empty, loading and error states. The seven baseline states are a minimum. Derive additional reachable states from actual interactions, including success/completion, selected/checked, expanded/collapsed, validation and read-only where applicable. Specify triggers, appearance, approved copy, semantics, announcements, keyboard/focus behavior and reference evidence. Success communicates the confirmed outcome and next action. The interaction critique fails when a reachable state or transition is unspecified. For every form, specify labels, required/optional indicators, accepted formats, help, validation timing, inline/summary errors, failure focus, input preservation and correction steps. Define submitting, success, failure, retry and duplicate-submission behavior. For consequential actions, specify cancellation, confirmation or undo as appropriate, plus unsaved-change behavior. Each applicable behavior requires approved interface copy and a task-level acceptance check; justify N/A. See the [handoff contract](../../references/handoff-contract.md). Also document language, direction, long-copy reflow and motion fallback. Preserve meaningful content and source-backed claims. In review mode, list evidence-backed copy, craft and WCAG 2.2 AA issues without altering source.
     9	
    10	## Gotchas
    11	
    12	- A vendor template or default palette never overrides the project's brief, approved wireframes or accessibility floor.
    13	- External sharing, generation with cost, or a design-system mutation needs Fadel's yes in Fannan's chat.
