release/UNTESTED.md:7:- **Compositing (R16-GPT-01):** `filter: opacity()` is composited like opacity; identity filters are ignored; any other filter function, a blend mode, a backdrop filter or a mask anywhere on the text's composed ancestor chain makes that text unknown (`contrastEffects`), and the cross-check is INCOMPLETE in either rendering. Consequence: a page that keeps such an effect on text cannot pass the integrity cross-check, by design. UNTESTED: effects on pseudo-elements or SVG text; `filter` values set through `url()` to an SVG filter that is in fact an identity (counted unknown); text painted inside a canvas.
release/UNTESTED.md:8:- **Native controls (R16-GPT-02):** values, placeholders (with the `::placeholder` colour), button-type input labels and a select's chosen option are contrast-checked; controls, links, images and elements with a role or ARIA label are compared with their accessible name and displayed value. The accessible name is an approximation of the specification (aria-labelledby, aria-label, label elements, value, alt, own text, title, placeholder), not the full algorithm. UNTESTED: `::file-selector-button`, date and time pickers, autofill colours, `<option>` lists while open, names from CSS generated content. As before, an unexplained JavaScript-off content difference records a content mismatch and the cross-check status is INCOMPLETE (R13 N14).
release/UNTESTED.md:9:- **Wireframe coverage (R16-GPT-03):** the wireframe phase requires each screen's page to exist, an applicable default rendering per declared language, manual records per screen and language, and renders each declared screen/language with phase-appropriate checks (no frame hash, type, accent, spacing or placeholder thresholds yet). Links inside the pages (navigation between screens) are not followed.
release/UNTESTED.md:25:- **Content and contrast (R14-GPT-01/02):** copy slots and headings count as rendered when their text ranges have area (`display: contents`, zero-size boxes); contrast walks open shadow roots and resolves backgrounds through slots and hosts. UNTESTED: text inside closed shadow roots (fails as an unscanned scope in the width screen, not in the contrast diagnostic); backgrounds painted by a slotted element's light-DOM ancestors that the slot's own composed chain does not include.
release/UNTESTED.md:26:- **Width screen (R14-GPT-03/04):** closed shadow roots are counted at each width after a bounded settle (two animation frames or 250 ms); a viewport that cannot scroll vertically (html, or a propagated body, with `overflow: hidden`/`clip`) fails text and media below its bottom edge unless an inner scroller holds them. UNTESTED: a closed root created later than the settle; `position: sticky` content; horizontal reach on a hidden viewport beyond the existing overflow check.
release/UNTESTED.md:35:- **Frames (N04, N05, N21):** `iframe`, `frame`, `object`, `embed`, `fencedframe` and `portal` are nested scopes. Same-origin frames are partially inspected, for glass and width only, and every one of them fails the final handoff (DEFERRED in wireframes); there are no frame exceptions (q1). UNTESTED: no test renders a `fencedframe` or `portal`; only their presence in the selectors is checked.
release/UNTESTED.md:36:- **Width screen (N01-N03, N15, N16):** body overflow that propagates to the viewport, zero-size and `display: contents` wrappers, shadow text clipped by its host, keyboard reach across a table and closed shadow roots (counted through CDP, reported as unscanned) were each reproduced and fixed. UNTESTED: a closed shadow root inside a frame; CDP counting when DevTools domains are unavailable is reported as unscanned, not exercised.
release/UNTESTED.md:37:- **Stylesheets (N07):** `data:` and `blob:` stylesheets are refused; a stylesheet the probe cannot read and the checker did not serve fails. UNTESTED: `@import` chains deeper than one level in shadow roots.
release/UNTESTED.md:38:- **Known limits, raw glass (N08/N09):** `\xNN`, `\uNNNN` and `\u{...}` escapes are decoded and the raw and comment-stripped text are both matched. Not covered (obfuscation, out of the threat model): string concatenation (`'backdrop-' + 'filter'`), `String.fromCharCode`, `atob`, computed property names, template literals assembled at run time, and CSS built from variables in script. The computed-style check and the JavaScript-off pass remain the defences.
release/UNTESTED.md:39:- **Known limits, reduced motion (N17, N18):** the native `requestAnimationFrame` is bound at install, and `Function.prototype.call`/`apply`/`bind` and `Reflect.apply` are in the native-function check; page and states share one routine. Not covered: a page that hides patches from `Function.prototype.toString` (heuristic; the between-world comparison remains), rAF called from an `about:blank` child frame created after the init script, and animation started by timers after the 700 ms window.
release/UNTESTED.md:40:- **Integrity (N11-N14, N19):** the vector now carries every hard-fail input (accent ratios, filler, rule of three, frames, unscanned stylesheets and scopes, per-width maps, contrast unknown/coverage); content compares slot and heading text; a content waiver is INCOMPLETE, never PASS; the native-function check has no default. UNTESTED: JavaScript-off equivalence for content inserted by CSS (`content:` on pseudo-elements).
release/UNTESTED.md:41:- **Shadow DOM (N20):** spacing, design counters, placeholders, h1 and the copy walker use the composed tree including open shadow roots. UNTESTED: slotted light-DOM content assigned to named slots in nested shadow trees.
release/UNTESTED.md:42:- **Package (N10, q2):** a credential word anywhere in a path part is refused (except three reviewed tool, test and evidence names); `tokens.json` passes only where the `handoff.json` beside it declares that path and hash and the content is design tokens; a stdlib content screen refuses obvious secrets (private-key blocks, cloud and chat tokens, OAuth secret values) in every packaged or hashed file. Known limit: secrets in formats the screen does not know, and binary files.
release/UNTESTED.md:48:- **Accent area and stray colours (M19, closed):** the accent check binds the declared variable to the approved token only. Accent area and coverage are approximate (a DOM background-area proxy) and are decided by screenshots and the manual `accent-area` and `palette` reviews (panel A). A page that paints large areas in another, unapproved colour is NOT failed automatically. UNTESTED by design.
release/UNTESTED.md:49:- **Frames (M03):** any frame (same-origin, `data:`, sandboxed or cross-origin) fails the final handoff and is recorded as DEFERRED in wireframes, because axe and the probes run in the main frame only. The R11 line below that called such frames "blocked" was wrong: they were recorded, not gated. Frame content is still not inspected (a frame is a stop, not a scan). *(Superseded by R13 N21: frames are partially inspected, for glass and width, and every frame, object, embed or fencedframe fails the handoff.)*
release/UNTESTED.md:51:- **Integrity (M06-M08, M17):** the full hard-fail vector (glass, h1, placeholders, centred, type sizes, hero gradient, purple-blue, icon rows, accent, spacing off-scale, overflow, clipped, offscreen-left, unreachable, scrolled text, unmeasured, reflow, contrast) is compared page world vs probe world and with JavaScript off, on the positional page and on every declared state. Contrast is a custom diagnostic (text vs resolved solid background, 4.5:1 / 3:1), not axe: axe cannot run with JavaScript off. JavaScript-off content (visible copy slots, h1 count, lang, dir) must match or the cross-check is INCOMPLETE. UNTESTED: text over images or gradients in the contrast diagnostic (counted as unknown, not failed); the native-function check stays a heuristic.
release/UNTESTED.md:52:- **320 px reflow (M01, M02, M09-M11, M14):** scrollers are measured with their own text, open shadow roots and same-origin frames; content outside a scroller's reachable range is `unreachable` at every width; keyboard use means an explicit `tabindex >= 0` scroller or usable targets that step across the whole extent; candidates and their exceptions are scoped to screen/state/lang. UNTESTED: closed shadow roots, `overflow: overlay`, scroll snapping, and whether a resolved candidate genuinely needs 2D layout (the reviewer's decision). *(Superseded in part by R13 N21: same-origin frames are partially inspected and fail the handoff anyway.)*
release/UNTESTED.md:54:- **Spacing (M15, M20):** `html` and `body` margins are screened; every `data-fannan-spacing-exception` needs a scoped handoff `spacingExceptions` entry naming the approver. UNTESTED: exceptions on pseudo-elements.
release/UNTESTED.md:63:- **Glass (S2/C6, panel D):** computed on `html`, `body`, visible elements and rendered pseudo-elements, in open shadow roots and same-origin (srcdoc) frames, plus constructed stylesheets and raw-text scans of served CSS/HTML/SVG/JS, style attributes and `<style>`. Any raw `backdrop-filter` other than `none` fails, even when the rule never applies (fail closed). NOT COVERED: closed shadow roots (unreachable from script) and cross-origin frames (blocked by the checker; listed as `unscannedFrames`). `file://` frames are cross-origin in Chrome, so their glass is caught only by the served-file text scan. A `-webkit-` alias added by a script in a constructed sheet is caught only by that text scan (Chrome drops it when parsing). Styles injected later than the probes run are UNTESTED. *(Superseded by R13 N21: frames are partially inspected and every frame fails the handoff.)*
release/UNTESTED.md:65:- **Probe world and integrity (C3, panel C):** probes and axe run in a CDP isolated world (not a Playwright API). The page-world vs probe-world comparison, the native-function check (a heuristic: a page can hide a patch from `toString`) and the JavaScript-off pass run on the positional page only, not on every state. The JavaScript-off pass compares glass and the 320 px screen. Contrast is NOT cross-checked with JavaScript off, because axe does not complete with page scripts disabled in Chrome 155. Iframes get no isolated world of their own. Page scripts that change the DOM or CSS between the two world measurements could cause a false mismatch (UNTESTED).
release/UNTESTED.md:72:- **Width screen (ARGON-R5-02, -05):** `body` and `overflow: clip` boxes are screened; text or media past the left edge fails. Chrome 155 headless only. Not tested: content pushed off the right edge inside a clipping ancestor other than `body` (reported only if it carries text and that box overflows), `transform`-based off-screen content in other browsers, and sr-only variants other than the 1×1 px, `clip: rect(0 0 0 0)` and `clip-path: inset(50%)` patterns (other variants may be reported and need a manual decision). Skip links are exempt only when focusable, absolute or fixed, and wholly left of the viewport; whether they become visible on focus is left to the focus probe and manual review.
release/UNTESTED.md:78:- **Accent colour (R9 sibling):** normalised by a detached canvas. Chrome 155 only; colour spaces beyond sRGB (oklch outside sRGB) may round differently from computed backgrounds. UNTESTED.
release/UNTESTED.md:98:- **ARGON-R2-09 design probe:** accent fallback, stock-glass gate and centred icon trios in any wrapper are checked in real Chrome 155 headless (test-only, unpinned). The trio rule is a screen: three icon-led items centred on the row or on every item. Reviewers still judge layouts it cannot see (CSS background icons, canvas, images without icon markup).
release/UNTESTED.md:104:- **R4-3 focus screen:** checked in real Chrome 154 headless on Mi'mar's box (test-only, unpinned browser; `test-results/r4/R4-3-chrome-*.log`). R4 composited colours over white, which could pass an invisible dark indicator on a dark page (a false pass) and fail a light one (a false fail). OPUS-R2-02 (R5) composites over the nearest opaque ancestor background captured unfocused, with a white fallback; checked in real Chrome (`test-results/r5/OPUS-02-chrome-*.log`). Background images, gradients, `opacity`, filters, blend modes and content painted behind via positioning are not modelled; pseudo-elements are measured against the element's backdrop, not its own background. Manual focus review stays required. The 3:1 threshold is a screening choice for reviewers to confirm; it does not prove WCAG 2.4.7/2.4.11/2.4.13 or 1.4.11.
release/UNTESTED.md:115:- **Actual browser focus rendering: NOT ESTABLISHED.** Chrome CLI attempt with an isolated temporary profile aborted with signal 6 in sandbox. Before/after computed-style logic is unit-tested; real browser/WCAG/manual focus, appearance contrast, overlays and screenshot behavior remain untested. No no-sandbox fallback was used.
